device_id,image_id
# Which device should have which image. Apply with: tools/apply-assignments.sh
#
# Comment lines (#) and the header are ignored, so every example row below is
# inert until you uncomment it. Addresses are TEST-NET-1 (192.0.2.0/24, RFC
# 5737) placeholders -- replace them with your own device ids.
#
# Changing a device's row to a different image makes that device pull the new
# image (within ~60s of applying) and PARK the old one: its torrent stops and
# its staging copy is freed, but the copy already placed on the storage root is
# deliberately KEPT so re-adding the image is a presence check rather than
# another multi-gigabyte transfer. That kept copy is reclaimed by a later
# placement that is short of room -- not at the moment you reassign -- so size
# the storage root for the images you want resident at once. See
# docs/zensical/device-agents.md ("Unassigned image park").
#192.0.2.10,cat9k_iosxe.26.01.01
#192.0.2.20,cat9k_iosxe.26.01.01
#192.0.2.30,cat9k_iosxe.26.01.01
